    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18990" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαδ-ιστικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>good at walking,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				128
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				180
			</span></i>; <i>able to walk,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Simp.
				<u>in Ph.</u>
				887.17
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ β.</span>”
				<i>that which is capable of walking,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Int.</u>
					21b16
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποὺς . . ὄργανον β.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					<u>UP</u>
					2.9
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Gaur.</u>
					1.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>for riding animals,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στάβλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					146.1
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(vi A. D.)</span>.</div>
